	.4byte 12
gBwText_146_0:
	.string "Man oh man...\nWhat is going on today?\pChallengers coming one\nright after another.\pWell, no matter.\pI am Grimsley of the Elite Four, and I\nwill fulfill my duty to be your opponent.$"
gBwText_146_1:
	.string "Whether or not you get to fight at full\nstrength, whether or not luck smiles\lon you--none of that matters.\pOnly results matter. And a loss is a\nloss.\pSee, victory shines like a bright light.\pAnd right now, you and your Pokémon\nare shining brilliantly.$"
gBwText_146_2:
	.string "Now, I'm nothing more than\nthe guy who lost...\pNothing more, nothing less.\nSigh...\pYou should take that strength and test\nit against the rest of the Elite Four.$"
gBwText_146_3:
	.string "Astonishing!\pYou have defeated every member of\nthe Pokémon League's Elite Four.\pBut it isn't over yet.\pThere is one more opponent against\nwhom you must prove your strength.\pThe pinnacle of the Pokémon League,\nthe Champion, Alder...\pOr, perhaps, that man called N has\ndefeated him and taken his title.\pI don't know which one you will face,\nbut check the statue in the central\lplaza, and continue to the final room.$"
gBwText_146_4:
	.string "Life is a serious battle, and you have\nto use the tools you're given.\pIt's more important to master the\ncards you're holding than to complain\labout the ones your opponents were\ldealt.\pLet us begin.\nAnd may the best Trainer win!\pContests like this are proof\nthat you are really living...$"
gBwText_146_5:
	.string "There are bad ways to win--\nand good ways to lose.\pWhat's interesting and troubling is\nthat it's not always clear which is\lwhich.\pA flipped coin doesn't always land\nheads or tails.\pSometimes it may never land at all...$"
gBwText_146_6:
	.string "Excellent!\pThe nice thing about Pokémon battles is\nthey teach the loser something, as well.\pThat said...\nYou should take that strength and test\lit against the rest of the Elite Four!$"
gBwText_146_7:
	.string "Astonishing!\pYou have defeated every member of\nthe Pokémon League's Elite Four.\pBut it isn't over yet.\pThere is one more opponent against\nwhom you must prove your strength.\pCheck the statue in the central plaza,\nand continue to the final room.$"
	.align 2
	.global gBwTextTable_146
