	.4byte gBwText_363_8
	.global gBwTextCount_363
gBwTextCount_363:
	.4byte 9
gBwText_364_0:
	.string "This is the Season Research Lab.\pTwist Mountain, just beyond Mistralton,\nhas snow, depending on the season.$"
gBwText_364_1:
	.string "Some Pokémon change their appearance\ndepending on the season.\pCould that also be considered\na type of evolution?$"
gBwText_364_2:
	.string "We research changes in nature that\noccur due to the seasons.\pConsider the Pokémon called\n{STR_VAR_1}, which lives in this forest.\pIts appearance is said to change\naccording to the season.\pThis characteristic is of great\ninterest to us.\pWe want to research this Pokémon and\nobserve its seasonal changes.\pThat's why we developed a marvelous\nclimate-control system that\ltranscends the seasons and allows us\lto freely adjust temperature and\lhumidity!$"
gBwText_364_3:
	.string "Up to this point, everything has been\nfine...but we are very busy, and we\lhaven't really had a chance to catch\lmany {STR_VAR_1} to study.\pSo, this is what we would like to ask\nyou. First, please capture a\l{STR_VAR_1}.\pThen, when its appearance changes,\ncould you bring it back to the lab?\pThen, when we've confirmed the change\nto the {STR_VAR_1} you bring us, we will\lalso go search for that season's\l{STR_VAR_1}.$"
gBwText_364_4:
	.string "How about it?\pIf you don't mind, would you please\nshow us what {STR_VAR_1} looks like\lnow?$"
gBwText_364_5:
	.string "{STR_VAR_1}'s Spring Form!\pThe luster of its body and its coloring\nis like a flower field in the spring!\pThe scent emanating from it is also\nvery floral.\pThank you so much! I want to go catch\nmy own {STR_VAR_1} right away!$"
gBwText_364_6:
	.string "{STR_VAR_1}'s Summer Form!\pThe luster of its body and its coloring\nis like a thicket in summer!\pThe scent emanating from it is also\nvery fresh and green.\pThank you so much! I want to go catch\nmy own {STR_VAR_1} right away!$"
gBwText_364_7:
	.string "{STR_VAR_1}'s Autumn Form!\pThe luster of its body and its coloring\nis like a tree-lined road with falling\lleaves dancing down!\pThe scent emanating from it is also\nlike dry leaves.\pThank you so much! I want to go catch\nmy own {STR_VAR_1} right away!$"
gBwText_364_8:
	.string "{STR_VAR_1}'s Winter Form.\pThe luster of its body and its coloring\nis like the slope of a mountain!\pThe scent emanating from it\nis also like fresh snow.\pThank you so much! I want to go catch\nmy own {STR_VAR_1} right away!$"
gBwText_364_9:
	.string "Thank you very much!\pBut we've already caught\nthat Form of {STR_VAR_1}.$"
gBwText_364_10:
	.string "Oh, I see.\pWe would be really grateful if you could\nassist us with our research, but if\lyou're too busy...$"
gBwText_364_11:
	.string "Oh! It's you!\pThanks to you, we've caught all of\nthe Forms of {STR_VAR_1}.\pNow we can thoroughly study the\nrelationship between Pokémon, seasons,\land climate.\pThank you very much.\nIt isn't much, but please accept this.$"
gBwText_364_12:
	.string "This is the only place in the world where\nyou can see {STR_VAR_1}'s four\lseasonal Forms all at one time.\pThey've kind of become our mascots!$"
gBwText_364_13:
	.string "I hate to say this, but that Pokémon is\nnot the {STR_VAR_1} we're looking for.$"
gBwText_364_14:
	.string "Dreee!$"
gBwText_364_15:
	.string "Dreee! Dree dree!$"
gBwText_364_16:
	.string "Dreen! Droooon!$"
gBwText_364_17:
	.string "Droon...$"
gBwText_364_18:
	.string "The temperature and humidity\ninside the case next to me\lare controlled by a machine.$"
gBwText_364_19:
	.string "The glass is slightly cold to the touch.\pThe plants inside the case\nhave grown some pretty Berries.$"
gBwText_364_20:
	.string "The glass is very cold to the touch.\pThe plants inside the case\nhave lost all their leaves.$"
gBwText_364_21:
	.string "The glass is slightly warm to the touch.\pThe plants inside the case\nhave grown small buds.$"
gBwText_364_22:
	.string "The glass is very warm to the touch.\pThe plants inside the case\nhave big, healthy leaves.$"
gBwText_364_23:
	.string "Route 6's temperature {STR_VAR_1} ?C$"
gBwText_364_24:
	.string "Route 6's temperature {STR_VAR_1} ?C$"
gBwText_364_25:
	.string "Route 6's temperature {STR_VAR_1} ?C$"
gBwText_364_26:
	.string "Route 6's temperature -{STR_VAR_1} ?C$"
	.align 2
