gBwText_462_0:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\pIt's the success story of the rookie\nPokémon Trainer, {STR_VAR_1}, who set\lout on a journey to become the\lChampion a year ago!$"
gBwText_462_1:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 1: “Nicknaming is Tough!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, he had thought of\nnicknames for {STR_VAR_2} Pokémon!$"
gBwText_462_2:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 2: “Strenuous Saving!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, his number of saved\ngames is {STR_VAR_2}!$"
gBwText_462_3:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 3: “Pokémon Center,\lPokémon Healer”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, his number of visits to\nthe Pokémon Center is {STR_VAR_2}!$"
gBwText_462_4:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 4: “Shop 'til You Drop!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, his total spent is\n${STR_VAR_3} after this many shopping\ltrips: {STR_VAR_2}!$"
gBwText_462_5:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 5: “TV Pride!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, his number of\nTV-watching experiences is\l{STR_VAR_2}!$"
gBwText_462_6:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 6: “Catch Pokémon If You Can!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, he had caught\n{STR_VAR_2} Pokémon!$"
gBwText_462_7:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 7: “Sometimes Ya Gotta Fight!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, he had battled\n{STR_VAR_2} Pokémon\land this many Trainers: {STR_VAR_3}!$"
gBwText_462_8:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 8: “Evolved at Last!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, he had evolved\n{STR_VAR_2} Pokémon!$"
gBwText_462_9:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 9: “Turn Fishing Line\lto Clothesline!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, he had reeled in\n{STR_VAR_2} Pokémon and lost\l{STR_VAR_3} Pokémon!$"
gBwText_462_10:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 10: “The Champion!!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, he had fought in\n{STR_VAR_2} battles and entered the\lHall of Fame this many times:\l{STR_VAR_3}!$"
gBwText_462_11:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\pIt's the success story of the rookie\nPokémon Trainer, {STR_VAR_1}, who set\lout on a journey to become the\lChampion a year ago!$"
gBwText_462_12:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 1: “Nicknaming is Tough!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, she had thought of\nnicknames for {STR_VAR_2} Pokémon!$"
gBwText_462_13:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 2: “Strenuous Saving!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, her number of saved\ngames is {STR_VAR_2}!$"
gBwText_462_14:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 3: “Pokémon Center,\lPokémon Healer”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, her number of visits\nto the Pokémon Center is {STR_VAR_2}!$"
gBwText_462_15:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 4: “Shop 'til You Drop!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, her total spent is\n${STR_VAR_3} after this many\lshopping trips: {STR_VAR_2}!$"
gBwText_462_16:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 5: “TV Pride!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, her number of\nTV-watching experiences is\l{STR_VAR_2}!$"
gBwText_462_17:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 6: “Catch Pokémon If You Can!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, she had caught\n{STR_VAR_2} Pokémon!$"
gBwText_462_18:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 7: “Sometimes Ya Gotta Fight!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, she had battled\n{STR_VAR_2} Pokémon\land this many Trainers: {STR_VAR_3}!$"
gBwText_462_19:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 8: “Evolved at Last!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, she had evolved\n{STR_VAR_2} Pokémon!$"
gBwText_462_20:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 9: “Turn Fishing Line\lto Clothesline!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, she had reeled in\n{STR_VAR_2} Pokémon and lost\l{STR_VAR_3} Pokémon!$"
gBwText_462_21:
	.string "It's the cartoon\n“Pokémon Trainer {STR_VAR_1}!“\lEpisode 10: “The Champion!!”\pOur story begins...and then\nthings happen...\pAnd a year later, she had fought in\n{STR_VAR_2} battles and entered the\lHall of Fame this many times:\l{STR_VAR_3}!$"
gBwText_462_22:
	.string "The Number One “Bicycle“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, ridden a Bicycle\lthis many times: {STR_VAR_2}!\pHow about it, {STR_VAR_1}?\pIsn't the breeze you feel when\npedaling a Bicycle just the best?$"
gBwText_462_23:
	.string "The Number One “Egg“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, hatched this many\lEggs: {STR_VAR_2}!\pHow about it, {STR_VAR_1}?\pIsn't the sight of a Pokémon hatching\na fantastic spectacle?$"
gBwText_462_24:
	.string "The Number One “Day Care“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, left {STR_VAR_2} Pokémon at\lthe Day Care!\pHow about it, {STR_VAR_1}?\pDo you have a crush on someone who\nworks at the Day Care? Hmmm?$"
gBwText_462_25:
	.string "The Number One “GTS“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, left {STR_VAR_2} Pokémon\lwith the GTS!\pThat's fantastic, {STR_VAR_1}!\nYou are truly a global Trainer!!$"
gBwText_462_26:
	.string "The Number One “Mail Writing“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, written Mail this many\ltimes: {STR_VAR_2}!\pThat's fantastic, {STR_VAR_1}!\nThe feelings communicated by Mail...\lThey are wonderful, aren't they?$"
gBwText_462_27:
	.string "The Number One “Premier Ball“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, received this many\lPremier Balls: {STR_VAR_2}!\pThat's fantastic, {STR_VAR_1}!\nYou're quite the skilled shopper!$"
gBwText_462_28:
	.string "The Number One “Stay at Home“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, rested at home this many\ltimes: {STR_VAR_2}!\pThat's fantastic, {STR_VAR_1}!\nAfter all, there's no place like home.$"
gBwText_462_29:
	.string "The Number One “Splash“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, used the move Splash\lthis many times: {STR_VAR_2}!\pWhat's up with that, {STR_VAR_1}?\nIs Splash really that amusing?$"
gBwText_462_30:
	.string "The Number One “Struggle“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, used the move Struggle\lthis many times: {STR_VAR_2}!\pThat's amazing, {STR_VAR_1}!\nThat's the never-give-up spirit!$"
gBwText_462_31:
	.string "The Number One “Had No Effect“\nTrainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, used a move that has no\leffect on an opponent this many\ltimes: {STR_VAR_2}!\pIt can't be helped, {STR_VAR_1}!\nPokémon type matchups are difficult!$"
gBwText_462_32:
	.string "The Number One “Can't Escape“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, failed to run away this many\ltimes: {STR_VAR_2}!\pIt can't be helped, {STR_VAR_1}!\nThat's life!$"
gBwText_462_33:
	.string "The Number One\n“Missed Opportunity“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, had {STR_VAR_2} Pokémon get\laway!\pIt can't be helped, {STR_VAR_1}!\nI'm sure you'll see them again someday!$"
gBwText_462_34:
	.string "The Number One “Extracting“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, extracted {STR_VAR_2}\lPokémon from Fossils!\pHow about it, {STR_VAR_1}?\nDo you feel the mystery of history?$"
gBwText_462_35:
	.string "The Number One “Spin Trade“ Trainer!\pAccording to our independent research,\nNuvema Town's {STR_VAR_1} has,\lamazingly, traded Eggs with Spin Trade\lthis many times: {STR_VAR_2}!\pHow about it, {STR_VAR_1}?\nSpin, spin, spin some more, right?$"
gBwText_462_36:
	.string "This is the documentary “The Best Day.“\pToday, we will discuss a Trainer named\n{STR_VAR_1}, who defeated {STR_VAR_2}\lPokémon in a single day!\pThis Trainer is definitely concerned\nonly with the search for Pokémon.$"
gBwText_462_37:
	.string "This is the documentary “The Best Day.“\pToday, we will discuss a Trainer named\n{STR_VAR_1}, who caught {STR_VAR_2}\lPokémon in a single day!\pThis Trainer is doing nothing but\nthrowing Poké Balls.$"
gBwText_462_38:
	.string "This is the documentary “The Best Day.“\pToday, we will discuss a Trainer named\n{STR_VAR_1}, who defeated this many\lTrainers in a single day: {STR_VAR_2}!\pThis Trainer definitely thinks battling\nother Trainers is the most fun ever!$"
gBwText_462_39:
	.string "This is the documentary “The Best Day.“\pToday, we will discuss a Trainer named\n{STR_VAR_1}, who evolved {STR_VAR_2}\lPokémon in a single day!\pThis Trainer surely loves the moment\nof evolution.$"
gBwText_462_40:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the\lmove Quash.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pQuash is a fantastically stubborn move\nthat makes the target's move go last.\pAs for how to use it in life... If, for\nexample, someone you are dating\lis about to break up with you...\pWell, you can see how using this move\nquickly could exhibit dramatic effects!\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until next\ntime...good-bye!$"
gBwText_462_41:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about\lthe move Venoshock.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pVenoshock covers the target in a\nspecial kind of poisonous liquid. It's a\ltruly spicy move!\pAs for how to use it in life... Sometimes,\nwhen you're cooking, your dish just\lneeds a little extra pinch of something.\pWell, you can see how using this move\nquickly could add a dangerous flavor!\pAnnouncer: I see.\nI sure learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone,\nuntil next time, good-bye!$"
gBwText_462_42:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lLow Sweep.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pLow Sweep is a simple but wild move.\nIt's a swift kick to the lower part of\lthe target's legs.\pIt can also be handy in everyday life.\nJust imagine a lady wearing a short\lskirt, and she has to kick someone...\pShe can use this move without causing\nany embarrassment to herself.\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until next\ntime, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_43:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lHone Claws.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pHone Claws is a very clean move where\nthe user's claws are honed and\lsharpened.\pLadies could use this move in everyday\nlife. It's like a super-powered\lmanicure!\pAnnouncer: I see.\nI sure learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone,\nuntil next time, good-bye!$"
gBwText_462_44:
	.string "Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lSmack Down.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pSmack Down is a classic and primitive\nmove where something is thrown at a\lflying target to bring it to the ground.\pThere's an effective use for this move\nin everyday life.\pFor example, suppose you sent air mail\nto someone, but then you change your\lmind and don't want them to read it!\pYou could use this move to knock it\ndown before it gets to them.\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until next\ntime, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_45:
	.string "Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“ Today,\nwe will learn about the move Psyshock.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pPsyshock is a very indirect move where\nthe user attacks with a psychic wave\lthat takes physical form.\pIt can be used effectively in everyday\nlife, too.\pFor example, sometimes you want\nto practice comedy routines\lby yourself, right?\pIf you time this move right, you can\nsmack yourself around for some\lamazing physical comedy!\pAnnouncer: I see.\nI sure learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until next\ntime, good-bye!$"
gBwText_462_46:
	.string "Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lEchoed Voice.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pEchoed Voice is a very rugged move\nwhose power grows when you use it in\lsuccessive turns.\pI bet you can think of ways to use this\nmove in everyday life without my help!\pYou know how sometimes you have to tell\nyour kids the same thing over and over\lbefore they listen?\pIn this situation, parents, teachers,\nand friends can all use this move and it\lwill be very effective!\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until next\ntime, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_47:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lFoul Play.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pFoul Play is a move that gets better\nthe more physically strong your\lopponent is.\pIt's a little sneaky, but you can use it\nin everyday life. For example, if you're\lterrible at sports, and you're going up\lagainst a big, powerful opponent...\pWell, it might be considered cheating,\nbut it would get the job done!\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until next\ntime, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_48:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lSky Drop.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pSky Drop is a dramatic move where the\ntarget is taken high into the sky and\lthen slammed into the ground.\pThere's an effective use for this move\nin everyday life: Showing off!\pYou could use this move on\nyourself, right? If you go fluttering up\linto the sky, you'll impress everyone!\pIt's an extremely dramatic\nperformance! Just brace yourself for\lthe landing...\pAnnouncer: Oh dear, that sounds\ndangerous... Ahem. Well, I learned a lot.\pOK then, everyone, until next\ntime, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_49:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lGuard Split.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pGuard Split is a very balanced move\nthat takes the defensive power of both\lsides and divides it up evenly.\pHere's a practical application. If you\nand a friend get lost in the mountains,\lyou could use this move to share your\ldefenses so you can both withstand\lthe cold.\pIt's a great way to test the dynamics\nof a relationship!\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until next\ntime, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_50:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lSimple Beam.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pSimple Beam is a very educational move\nthat changes the target's Ability to\lSimple, where stat changes are doubled.\pHere's how to use it in everyday life...\pSuppose a meeting at work is dragging\non and on.\pJust use this move quickly on all the\nparticipants. If they're all Simple,\lthey'll start thinking the same way,\lthe meeting will be over twice as fast!\pMight not accomplish much, though...\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until next\ntime, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_51:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lAfter You.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pAfter You is a move filled with the\nspirit of give and take, where you allow\lthe target to attack right after you\ldo.\pIn practical terms, if you see a new\ndish at a restaurant that you're a\llittle nervous about, you can use this\lmove to make someone else taste it\lfirst!\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until next\ntime, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_52:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lQuiver Dance.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pQuiver Dance is a beautiful, graceful\nmove that raises the user's Sp. Atk,\lSp. Def, and Speed stats.\pThere's an effective use for this move\nin everyday life. For example, suppose\lyou were invited to your friend's\lbirthday, but you forgot to bring a\lgift.\pYou could use this move when you arrive\nat the party, as a distraction...\lAnd then it would make you harder\lto hit if your friend got angry!\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until next\ntime, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_53:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lChip Away.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pChip Away is a very persistent move\nthat keeps striking and ignores all of\lthe target's stat changes.\pIn everyday life, this move might be\nhandy for winning an argument with\la really stubborn person!\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until next\ntime, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_54:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lReflect Type.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pReflect Type is a very conformist move\nthat makes your type match your\ltarget's type.\pThis works really well if you're\nspending time with someone and you\ldecide you have nothing in common. Use\lthis move and... Voilà! Instant common\lground!\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until\nnext time, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_55:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the\lmove Synchronoise.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pSynchronoise is an exclusive move that\nonly attacks everything of the same\ltype as the user.\pIf a person who has the same\npersonality and characteristics as you\lshows up at school or work, you could\luse this move to distinguish yourself.\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until\nnext time, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_56:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lBestow.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pBestow is a very generous move where\nyou pass an item to the target.\pThere's an effective use for this move\nin everyday life.\pSometimes you receive a gift that will\nclearly cause trouble, right?\pYou can use this move right away to...\nNo, actually, you'd better wait until\lthe person who gave you the gift has\lleft!\pBut then you can use the move to pass\nyour unwanted gift off to someone else.\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until\nnext time, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_57:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lMagic Room.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pMagic Room is a very basic move that\ncauses items to have no effect for a\lcertain amount of turns.\pThere's an effective use for this move\nin everyday life.\pFor example, suppose a child is begging\nyou to buy a toy. If you use this move\lat the exact moment the child\lpicks up the toy, it will counter the\l“I want this” effect!\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until\nnext time, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_58:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lShell Smash.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pShell Smash is a possibly risky move\nwhere the user's Speed, Attack, and\lSp. Atk stats increase at the expense\lof defensive power.\pThere's an effective use for this move\nin everyday life.\pFor example, how about when you switch\nto a new school?\pThis move could be the brand-new\nstart you might need.\lIt could change your whole life!\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until\nnext time, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_59:
	.string "Announcer: Good evening, ladies\nand gentlemen!\pIt's time for “Moves for Living.“\nToday, we will learn about the move\lSoak.\pOur guest expert is\nDr. Technic Al'Machine,\la professor at Castelia University.\pAl'Machine: Hello. I'm Dr. Al'Machine.\pWell, Soak is a sloshy move that turns\nthe target into a Water type.\pWondering how you could possibly use\nthis move in everyday life?\pWhat if you spilled a drink during an\nimportant occasion? If you use this\lmove right, it might not matter at all!\pAnnouncer: I see...\nI learned a lot.\pWell then, everyone, until\nnext time, good-bye.$"
gBwText_462_60:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Contrary!\pContrary makes stat changes\ngo topsy-turvy!\pFor example, if a Pokémon with Contrary\ngets hit by a move that lowers its\lSpeed, it will have the opposite effect!\pThat's right. Its Speed will increase!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_61:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Cursed Body!\pIf a Pokémon with Cursed Body is\ndamaged by a move, sometimes that move\lcan be disabled so the foe can't use it\lanymore!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_62:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Weak Armor!\pWhen a Pokémon with Weak Armor is hit\nby a physical attack, its Defense will\lbe lowered, but its Speed will go up!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_63:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Moody!\pDuring a battle, Moody raises one stat\nand lowers another at the end of\leach turn.\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_64:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Analytic!\pAnalytic is great for slower Pokémon. If\na Pokémon with Analytic goes last in a\lbattle, its move's power will be\lboosted!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_65:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Rattled!\pIf a Pokémon with Rattled is hit by a\nGhost-, Dark-, or Bug-type move, its\lSpeed will go up!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_66:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Prankster!\pPrankster gives priority to status\nmoves like Screech!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_67:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Sheer Force!\pA Pokémon with Sheer Force gets a\npower boost for moves that normally\lhave additional effects, but the\ladditional effects won't occur!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_68:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Magic Bounce!\pMagic Bounce works like the move\nMagic Coat, but it's “on” all the time!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_69:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Harvest!\pIf a Pokémon with Harvest eats a Berry\nduring battle, the Berry may regenerate\lat the end of the turn!\pIt's like an all-you-can-eat\nBerry buffet!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_70:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Sturdy!\pOne-hit KO attacks don't work on a\nPokémon with Sturdy. It hangs on to\lthat one last HP!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_71:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Cloud Nine!\pCloud Nine is great for travelers.\nIt prevents effects from weather!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_72:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Pickup!\pA Pokémon with Pickup can get the\neffect of an item an opponent has\lused in battle.\pIt also picks up various items\nwhen it is not battling.\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_73:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Lightningrod!\pIf a Pokémon with Lightningrod is in\nbattle, any Electric-type move will hit\lit.\pAnd getting hit by an Electric-type\nmove boosts the Pokémon's Sp. Atk\lstat!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_74:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Mold Breaker!\pA Pokémon with Mold Breaker can\ncompletely ignore its opponent's\lAbility when attacking.\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_75:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Klutz!\pHeld items have no effect on a Pokémon\nwith Klutz. It could even hold an\lIron Ball without being weighed down!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_76:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Anticipation!\pIf the opponent has a supereffective\nmove or a one-hit KO move, Anticipation\lwill warn you so you can be prepared!\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_77:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Dry Skin!\pPokémon with Dry Skin just love water,\nbecause they recover HP if they get\lwet.\pSo if they get hit by a Water-type move\nor go out in the rain, they feel better!\pUnfortunately, Fire-type moves do\nextra damage and sunny days hurt, too.\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_78:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Download!\pA Pokémon with Download can take\nadvantage of its opponent's\lweaknesses.\pIf the opponent's Defense is lower\nthan its Sp. Def, the Pokémon's Attack\lwill be boosted.\pIf the opponent's Sp. Def is lower than\nits Defense, the Pokémon's Sp. Atk will\lbe boosted.\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_79:
	.string "It's “The Waving Weaving Walk“--\nWawalk for short!\pI wonder what kind of Pokémon\nwe'll meet today?\pOh, what's this?\nIt's a Pokémon with the\lAbility Damp!\pIf a Pokémon with Damp is in battle,\nmoves like Explosion and Selfdestruct\lcan't be used.\pWell, it'd sure be nice if I had\nan Ability like that...\lI wonder where I should walk next.$"
gBwText_462_80:
	.string "Lady: Hello!\nIt's time for the “What's That?“ show,\lwhere we talk about wonderful items!\pToday we are talking about\nthe Eviolite!\pWatchy Watchog,\nhave you heard of the Eviolite?\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Come on! Like I'd know!)\pLady: Amazing! You know it!\nOK, well, I'll explain it anyway!\pWhen you give the Eviolite to a\nPokémon that hasn't evolved yet...\pIts Defense and Sp. Def both rise\nsharply! Isn't that amazing?!\lSo, we'll see you later, then!\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(What? That was a really short show!)$"
gBwText_462_81:
	.string "Lady: Hello!\nIt's time for the “What's That?“ show,\lwhere we talk about wonderful items!\pToday we are talking about the\nFloat Stone!\pWatchy Watchog,\nhave you heard of the Float Stone?\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Come on! Of course I haven't!)\pLady: Amazing! You do know it!\nOK, well, I'll explain it anyway!\pWhen you give the Float Stone to a\nPokémon, its weight decreases!\pLet's try giving one to Watchy\nright now!\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Hey! Are you calling me fat?!)$"
gBwText_462_82:
	.string "Lady: Hello!\nIt's time for the “What's That?“ show,\lwhere we talk about wonderful items!\pToday we are talking about the\nRocky Helmet!\pWatchy Watchog,\nhave you heard of the Rocky Helmet?\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Come on! Of course I haven't!)\pLady: Amazing! You do know it!\nOK, well, I'll explain it anyway!\pWhen an attack does physical damage\nto a Pokémon holding the Rocky Helmet,\lthe attacker takes damage, too.\pI'll try it! So I put it on, like so, and...\nOK, Watchy, hit me with your best shot!\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(No fair! You're not a Pokémon!)$"
gBwText_462_83:
	.string "Lady: Hello!\nIt's time for the “What's That?“ show,\lwhere we talk about wonderful items!\pToday we are talking about the\nAir Balloon!\pWatchy Watchog, \nhave you heard of the Air Balloon?\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Come on! Of course I haven't!)\pLady: Amazing! You do know it!\nOK, well, I'll explain it anyway!\pAmazingly, a Pokémon holding the\nAir Balloon will float up in the air!\pThat means Ground-type moves won't\nwork against it at all!\pBut, the balloon pops if the Pokémon\ngets hit with an attack, so be careful!\lOh no! I popped it!!\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Hey! Nice one, clumsy!)$"
gBwText_462_84:
	.string "Lady: Hello!\nIt's time for the “What's That?“ show,\lwhere we talk about wonderful items!\pToday we are talking about the\nRed Card!\pWatchy Watchog,\nhave you heard of the Red Card?\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Come on! Of course I haven't!)\pLady: Amazing! You do know it!\nOK, well, I'll explain it anyway!\pWhen the Pokémon holding the Red Card\nis attacked, the attacker is thrown out\lof the battle.\pJust so you know, Watchy, I'm holding\na Red Card right now!\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Hey! I'm not going to attack you!)$"
gBwText_462_85:
	.string "Lady: Hello!\nIt's time for the “What's That?“ show,\lwhere we talk about wonderful items!\pToday we are talking about the\nRing Target!\pWatchy Watchog,\nhave you heard of the Ring Target?\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Come on! Of course I haven't!)\pLady: Amazing! You do know it!\nOK, well, I'll explain it anyway!\pIf a Pokémon holds the Ring Target,\neven attacks that would usually have\lno effect will hit it!\pThat reminds me, I have a present for\nyou, Watchy! Your very own Ring Target!\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Hey! That's not very nice!)$"
gBwText_462_86:
	.string "Lady: Hello!\nIt's time for the “What's That?“ show,\lwhere we talk about wonderful items!\pToday we are talking about the\nBinding Band!\pWatchy Watchog, \nhave you heard of the Binding Band?\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Come on! Of course I haven't!)\pLady: Amazing! You do know it!\nOK, well, I'll explain it anyway!\pThe Binding Band increases the\npower of binding moves, like Wrap!\lWell, that's it for today!\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Hey! That's it?!)$"
gBwText_462_87:
	.string "Lady: Hello!\nIt's time for the “What's That?“ show,\lwhere we talk about wonderful items!\pToday we are talking about the\nAbsorb Bulb!\pWatchy Watchog,\nhave you heard of the Absorb Bulb?\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Come on! Of course I haven't!)\pLady: Amazing! You do know it!\nOK, well, I'll explain it anyway!\pWhen a Pokémon holding an\nAbsorb Bulb is hit by a Water-type\lattack, its Sp. Atk stat goes up!\pBut you can only use it once. Here, you\ncan have this used one!\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Don't pawn your garbage off on me!)$"
gBwText_462_88:
	.string "Lady: Hello!\nIt's time for the “What's That?“ show,\lwhere we talk about wonderful items!\pToday we are talking about the\nCell Battery!\pWatchy Watchog, \nhave you heard of the Cell Battery?\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Come on! Of course I haven't!)\pLady: Amazing! You do know it!\nOK, well, I'll explain it anyway!\pWhen a Pokémon holding a\nCell Battery is hit by an Electric-type\lattack, its Attack stat goes up!\pBut you can only use it once. I already\nused mine, so I can't give it to you!\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(I didn't want it anyway!)$"
gBwText_462_89:
	.string "Lady: Hello!\nIt's time for the “What's That?“ show,\lwhere we talk about wonderful items!\pToday we are talking about the\nEject Button!\pWatchy Watchog, \nhave you heard of the Eject Button?\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Come on! Of course I haven't!)\pLady: Amazing! You do know it!\nOK, well, I'll explain it anyway!\pWhen a Pokémon holding an\nEject Button is hit by a move, it goes\lright back into its Poké Ball!\pSo if you use it right, you don't have\nto worry about switching during a\lbattle! I'll use it to make a quick\lescape!\pWatchy: Tch tch cha!\n(Hey! Where do you think you're going?!)$"
gBwText_462_90:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nJanuary, your sign\lis Sawsbuck!\pYou could be described as an\nhonest and serious person!\pI believe that you would never\nbetray your friends.\pTry to be a big-hearted person,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky item\nfor a Sawsbuck sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nCarry a White Flute!\pThe humorous tone will put a smile\non the faces around you!\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_91:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nFebruary, your sign\lis Simipour!\pYou could be described as a\nvery free-spirited and unique person!\pYou can attract the interest of those\naround you with your mysterious charm.\pTry to be a more empathetic person,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky item\nfor a Simipour sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nHave your Pokémon carry Mail!\pThe fun content of the Mail will put\nsmiles on the faces around you!\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_92:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nMarch, your sign\lis Alomomola!\pYou are very kind and caring, aren't\nyou? Everyone around you is saved by\lyour love.\pTry to be a strong and enduring person,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky item\nfor an Alomomola sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nCarry a Hard Stone!\pEveryone around you will understand\nyour kind, reliable aura.\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_93:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nApril, your sign\lis Whimsicott!\pYou could be described as hating to\nlose and having a strong sense of\ljustice.\pEveryone around you probably respects\nyour strong character.\pTry to be a kind and gentle person,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky item\nfor a Whimsicott sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nCarry a Hyper Potion!\pEveryone around you will appreciate\nyour generous kindness.\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_94:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nMay, your sign\lis Bouffalant!\pYou are a very calm and\nrelaxed person!\pEveryone feels at peace\nwhen they're around you.\pTry to be a little more assertive,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky item\nfor a Bouffalant sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nCarry an X Attack!\pEveryone around you will be surprised\nwhen you aggressively attack.\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_95:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nJune, your sign\lis Klink!\pYou are a very curious and fun person!\nEveryone is impressed by your\lknowledge.\pTry to be a strong and enduring person,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky tip\nfor a Klink sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nUse a slow Pokémon!\pYou'll overwhelm everyone\nwith a well-thought-out attack!\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_96:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nJuly, your sign\lis Crustle!\pYou are very intuitive and smart!\pYour businesslike mood makes\nthe entire room feel sharp.\pTry to be a better listener,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky item\nfor a Crustle sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nCarry a Dowsing MCHN!\pEveryone around you will be surprised\nwhen you find one item after another.\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_97:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nAugust, your sign\lis Braviary!\pYou are a hard worker, and you\ntake care of people!\pEveryone can relax when you're\non the job!\pTry to be a little more restrained,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky item\nfor a Braviary sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nCarry Calcium!\pRaise the Special Attack stat of a\nreserved Pokémon and everyone will be\lin awe of its aggressive attacking\lstyle!\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_98:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nSeptember, your sign\lis Gothorita!\pYou are good at reading\nthe room, aren't you?\pEveryone around you also agrees\nyour judgments are accurate!\pTry to be a more generous person,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky item\nfor a Gothorita sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nCarry an Xtransceiver!\pPeople will be comforted by you,\nbecause you're always concerned about\leveryone.\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_99:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nOctober, your sign\lis Lampent!\pYou have good sense and\nare a very balanced person!\pYou make evenhanded choices.\pTry to show an enthusiastic spirit,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky item\nfor a Lampent sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nCarry a Choice Scarf!\pIt's fashionable, and you will shine as\nyou attack with only one move!\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_100:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nNovember, your sign\lis Scolipede!\pYou are a fiery person with\nstrong beliefs!\pNo one can imitate the\nfire you have!\pTry to have a supple mind,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky item\nfor a Scolipede sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nCarry a White Herb!\pIts ability to heal anything and its\ncleanliness give you a\lsurprising charm!\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_101:
	.string "Host: It's time for today's\n“Personality Assessment and\lHoroscope“!\pSo what's today's star sign?\nDr. Astropoff, if you please!\pAstropoff: If you were born in\nDecember, your sign\lis Fraxure!\pYou work hard at everything\nand can do anything!\pPeople around you respect\nyour abilities.\pTry to be a polite person,\nand all will be well!\pHost: What's the lucky item\nfor a Fraxure sign?\pAstropoff: Weeell...\nCarry a Poké Ball!\pThe sight of you daringly closing in on\na Poké Ball capture is sure to change\lthe impression people have of you!\pHost: Thank you very much!\nSee you next time!$"
gBwText_462_102:
	.string "Jingle: Woo hoo! All right!\nIt's “The National Gymquirer“!\pPage: That's right!\nWe collect the hottest gossip about\lGym Leaders seen around town!\pHere is today's letter.\pFrom someone going by the name\nCafélover! Thank yooou!\p“Recently, I saw Striaton Gym's three\nGym Leaders, and they were all out of\lorder! Like, Chili was Cilan, and\lCilan was Cress!”\pHmmm. Well, I'm not saying you're crazy,\nbut...are you sure they weren't just\lstanding in front of a mirror?\p“The National Gymquirer“!\nWe eagerly await your letters!$"
gBwText_462_103:
	.string "Jingle: Woo hoo! All right!\nIt's “The National Gymquirer“!\pPage: That's right!\nWe collect the hottest gossip about\lGym Leaders seen around town!\pHere is today's letter.\pFrom someone going by the name\nBonadventure! Thank yooou!\p“I saw it... Lenora, in the middle of the\nnight...talking to bones in the museum!\lI also heard a man's guttural\llaugh... It was scary!”\pI see. Very horrific.\pBut, I'll bet it was just her husband,\nHawes. He has a weird laugh...\p“The National Gymquirer“!\nWe eagerly await your letters!$"
gBwText_462_104:
	.string "Jingle: Woo hoo! All right!\nIt's “The National Gymquirer“!\pPage: That's right!\nWe collect the hottest gossip about\lGym Leaders seen around town!\pHere is today's letter.\pFrom someone going by the name\nCompoundeyes Wrestler! Thank yooou!\p“When I went to meet Burgh.\nIt was like he had been licking the\lhoneycomb walls!\lThat guy likes to eat!”\pNow that is a surprise...\pBut, I wonder if he was just admiring\nhis own face\lreflected on those walls...\lThat's also weird though...\p“The National Gymquirer“!\nWe eagerly await your letters!$"
gBwText_462_105:
	.string "Jingle: Woo hoo! All right!\nIt's “The National Gymquirer“!\pPage: That's right!\nWe collect the hottest gossip about\lGym Leaders seen around town!\pHere is today's letter.\pFrom someone going by the name\nShocking Supermodel...\pHmmm, that sounds like a Gym Leader\nI know. Well, let's see...\p“The Gym Leader Elesa said that\nNimbasa's Pokémon can dance\la nimble bossa!\pNobody laughed, but I thought it was\nreally funny! What do you think?”\pHmmm... It really seems like Elesa needs\nto come up with a sneakier pen name.\lWell, whatever!\p“The National Gymquirer“!\nWe eagerly await your letters!$"
gBwText_462_106:
	.string "Jingle: Woo hoo! All right!\nIt's “The National Gymquirer“!\pPage: That's right!\nWe collect the hottest gossip about\lGym Leaders seen around town!\pHere is today's letter.\pFrom someone going by the name\nVeildrifter. Thank yooou!\p“You know how Gym Leader Clay never\ntakes off his hat? Well, the other day I\lfinally saw him take it off...\pAnd underneath his big hat was a fluffy\nknit hat! He wears two hats! Weird,\lhuh?”\pHmm... That seems like it would be\nway too warm!\pStill, I wonder if that isn't just\nClay's hair sticking up all funny...\p“The National Gymquirer“!\nWe eagerly await your letters!$"
gBwText_462_107:
	.string "Jingle: Woo hoo! All right!\nIt's “The National Gymquirer“!\pPage: That's right!\nWe collect the hottest gossip about\lGym Leaders seen around town!\pHere is today's letter.\pFrom someone going by the name\nPilotcandidate. Thank yooou!\p“I'm an aspiring Pilot\nwho is a huge fan of Skyla!\pI couldn't take it anymore, and I\npeeked into her Gym...and it looked like\lshe was flying with the propeller on her\lhead!\pIsn't that amazing?! Maybe she\ndoesn't even need a plane!”\pHmm... That is mysterious!\pStill, I wonder if she was just using the\ncannons in her Gym to fly...\p“The National Gymquirer“!\nWe eagerly await your letters!$"
gBwText_462_108:
	.string "Jingle: Woo hoo! All right!\nIt's “The National Gymquirer“!\pPage: That's right!\nWe collect the hottest gossip about\lGym Leaders seen around town!\pHere is today's letter.\pFrom someone going by the name\nTheFridge. Thank yooou!\p“Brycen is too cool! He's always acting\nlike Mr. Tough Guy, like he doesn't even\lfeel the cold...but recently, I heard him\lsneeze inside his chilly Gym!”\pI guess even a super-cool Gym Leader\ncan catch a cold. Feel better soon,\lBrycen!\p“The National Gymquirer“!\nWe eagerly await your letters!$"
gBwText_462_109:
	.string "Jingle: Woo hoo! All right!\nIt's “The National Gymquirer“!\pPage: That's right!\nWe collect the hottest gossip about\lGym Leaders seen around town!\pHere is today's letter.\pFrom someone going by the name\nMadame Scale. Thank yooou!\p“I'm from Opelucid City, and I just went\nhome for the first time in a long time.\pI saw Drayden and Iris counting up a big\nhandful of coins!\pIsn't that setting a bad example for\nkids, flaunting your wealth like that?”\pHmmm... That's living the high life!\pBut you know, the Opelucid Gym Badge is\nshiny like a coin... Maybe you saw wrong?\p“The National Gymquirer“!\nWe eagerly await your letters!$"
gBwText_462_110:
	.string "Azusa: KONNICHIWA, yo!\nAre you overflowing with GENKI?\pIt's time for this week's highly\nanticipated “KOUKAN TALK!“\pThis is today's phrase:\n“Your Pokémon is cute!”\pThis is a phrase you want to try out!\nSo, what's the right way to say it?\p“Kawaii Pokémon da ne!“\nKa-wah-ii po-kay-mon da nay!\pWith this you can flatter that\nperson you like! YATTA!\pTrading Pokémon internationally\nis sure great! Tee hee!\pOK, be sure to watch again!\nMATA KONDO!$"
gBwText_462_111:
	.string "Azusa: OSSU, everybody!\pAre you so GENKI it's causing\neveryone else trouble?\pIt's time for this week's highly\nanticipated “KOUKAN TALK!“\pThis is today's phrase:\n“Where did you come from?”\pThis is handy! You'll want to know\nwhere your opponent is from!\pIf you want to say this in\nJapanese, it's like this!\p“Doko kara kita no?“\nDo-ko ka-ra kee-ta no?\pAfter that, there's no doubt you'll\nhave fun talking about where you're\lfrom! Yeah!\pOK, so, MATA NE! Bye-bye!$"
gBwText_462_112:
	.string "Azusa: Yoo-hoo, MINNA!\pToday I'm a little wound up, so let's\nget this “KOUKAN TALK“ started!\pThis week's phrase is this:\n“What's your favorite Pokémon?”\pSo what will this sound like\nin Japanese?\p“Ichiban suki na Pokémon wa?“\nIi-chee-ban su-kee nah po-kay-mo-n\lwah?\pThen both of you will know about\nthe other's favorite!\pBy the way, my favorite Pokémon is\n{STR_VAR_3}!\pOK, see you later!\nJA NE! Have a good day! Mwah!$"
gBwText_462_113:
	.string "Azusa: Meowdy, MINNA!\nIt's time for “KOUKAN TALK!“\pToday's one phrase for communication\nis this:\p“Where did you find that?”\pThis phrase can be useful\nwhenever you need it!\pHAI! So this useful phrase goes\nlike this in Japanese!\p“Sore doko de mitsuketano?“\nSo-re do-ko de mee-tsu-kay-tah no?\pWhen I meet Trainers with a cute\n{STR_VAR_3}, I ask them\lthat right away!\pSo with that, MATA ITSUKA AIMASHO!\nAnd adios!$"
gBwText_462_114:
	.string "Azusa: Hello, MINNA!\nIt's time for “KOUKAN TALK!“\pThis week's phrase is:\n“Nice meeting you!”\pUse this when parting with someone\nyou just met!\pAt times like this, I say:\n“Shiri aete yokatta!“\lShee-ree ah-e-te yo-ka-ta!\pIt's even better when you say this\nalong with a firm handshake!\pOK, that's it for today!\nJA NE!$"
gBwText_462_115:
	.string "Azusa: OSSU, MINNA!\pYesterday, I fell in love with\na TOTTEMO KAWAII Pokémon\lin the Musical!\pThis is what you say at that time!\n“I became your fan!“\pAfter that, I told it this in Japanese.\n“Anata no fan ni narimashita!”\lAh-nah-ta no fan nee\lna-ri-ma-shee-ta!\pIt was cute!\nSo utterly KAWAII!\pMy beloved {STR_VAR_3}!\pYour double-flip jump is just\ntoo adorable to be legal!\pOn that note, I'm going to\nthe Musical again today! JA NE!$"
gBwText_462_116:
	.string "Azusa: HAAAAI! For good kids and\neven kids that are a little bad...\lIt's time for “KOUKAN TALK!“\pToday's phrase is perfect for when two\npeople's thoughts match up, as if\lby telepathy!\p“I was thinking the same thing!” “Chodo\nonaji koto kangaeteta!“ Choh-do\lo-na-gee ko-to ka-n-ga-eh-te-ta!\pWhen I say this, the conversation\nalways picks up steam, and then it\lcan't stop!\pFor that reason, that's it for today!\nJA MATA NE!$"
gBwText_462_117:
	.string "Azusa: Hello, MINNA!\nIt's time for “KOUKAN TALK!“\pAnother day, another step closer to\nmastering global communication!\p...Recently, on the way back from the\nMusical, someone said this to me:\p“Your Pokémon looks different!”\n“Kawatta Pokémon da ne!“\lKa-wa-tah po-kay-mo-n da ne!\pI thought it could be a joke, but when I\nlooked at {STR_VAR_3}...BIKKURI!\pIt was still wearing Props from the\nMusical! I forgot to take them off!\lOops! That would look strange!\pHAI! That's it for today!\nMATA AIMASHOU! See you!$"
gBwText_462_118:
	.string "Azusa: Hey, MINA-SAN!\nIt's time for “KOUKAN TALK!“\pToday, I'll teach you this question to\nask when you see a Pokémon that you\lare interested in!\p“Where did you catch that Pokémon?”\n“Sono Pokémon doko de tsukamaeta no?“\lSo-no po-kay-mo-n do-koh de\ltsu-ka-mah-e-ta no?\pThen you can go catch one for yourself!\pOK, that's it for today!\nMINNA, bye-bye!$"
gBwText_462_119:
	.string "Azusa: ...Ne, Toru?\nNinniku no nioi suru?\pKinou sa, oishii pasuta\ntabetanda kedo sa,\lninniku ga sugoku\lkiiteta no yo ne.\pIki wo tometeiru no\natashi no sei ja nai yo ne?\p...Toru? Nande, kyou wa\nsonna ni shizuka na no?\pSonnani niou?\nAre... Ee? Nani?\pWhat?! No way!\nWe're rolling?!\pH-hello, MINNA! P-please watch “KOUKAN\nTALK“ again, OK? SAYONARA!$"
gBwText_462_120:
	.string "Toru: Hey, everyone!\nHow ya doin'?\pHa ha! Whether you're feeling good or\nbad, it's time for “KOUKAN TALK!“\pThis week's phrase is:\n“Check out this Pokémon!”\pThis is like telling someone: Hey, have a\nlook at my Pokémon! It's so cool! Wooo!\pWhen you want to say that in\nJapanese, say this!\p“Kono Pokémon mite!“\nKo-no po-kay-mo-n mee-te!\pWith this, you can show off your\nPokémon to each other, right?\pOK, thanks for watching this week!\nMATA KONDO!$"
gBwText_462_121:
	.string "Toru: Hey hey, is everyone\nexplosively GENKI today?!\p“KOUKAN TALK“ comin' atcha!\pToday's single phrase for\ncommunication is...\p“Let me see your Pokédex!”\pTrainers are always interested in\nanother Trainer's Pokédex!\pThis is what you say in that situation!\n“Pokémon Zukan misete!“\pPo-kay-mo-n zu-ka-n mee-say-te!\pNow you can have a person who speaks\nJapanese show you their Pokédex! You\lhave that? URAYAMASHII ZE!\pOK, have a great day!\nMATA NE! MINNA!$"
gBwText_462_122:
	.string "Toru: YA! MINNA!\nAre you enjoying life?\pIt's time for this week's\n“KOUKAN TALK!“\pThis week's phrase is for asking\nyour excellent Pokémon rival\lsomething, yeah!\p“How many Badges have you got?”\n“Ikutsu bajji motteru?“\pIi-ku-tsu ba ji mo te-ru?\nYEAH!\pWith this, you can see how\nfar your rival has progressed!\pThrough Pokémon, everyone can be\nfriends and rivals!\pOn that note, I'm going to challenge\nthe Gyms and collect more Badges!\lMATA NE!$"
gBwText_462_123:
	.string "Toru: OSSU, MINNA!\pToday's “KOUKAN TALK“\nis a liiittle different than usual!\pWhy? Because today I'm having\na fantastic day!\pSo what I'm going to teach you in this\nfantastic mood is this, KORE!\p“Are you having a good time?”\pSo you're thinking, I want to talk to\nthat person! But what should I say?\pOK, my hypothetical, shy\nyoung man or woman!\lI've got the perfect phrase for you!\p“Tanoshinderu?“\nTa-no-shi-n-de-ru?\pThe perfect conversation starter!\nJust run with it from here!\pSo that's it for today!\nSee you! MATA NE, MINNA!$"
gBwText_462_124:
	.string "Toru: OSSU!\pRecently, I met an UTSUKUSHII\nwoman at a party!\pThe second I saw her, I thought\nI'd seen her before somewhere.\lBut I couldn't remember her name!\pSo, in this situation, I went up to her,\nand I said this:\p“Dokoka de atta koto arukke?“\nDo-ko-ka de a ta ko-to a-ru keh?\pIt means, “Have we met somewhere?”\pAnd what do you think she said to me?\p“What? I work with you every day.\nYou're not serious, right?“\pIYA! It was an all-prettied-up Azusa!\nSHIMATAAAA!\pSo, that's it for today's\n“KOUKAN TALK!”\p...I sure hope Azusa will start\ntalking to me again soon!$"
gBwText_462_125:
	.string "Toru: KONNICHIWA, MINNA!\pWe're getting back to the basics\non today's “KOUKAN TALK!“\pToday, we will introduce a very\nbasic phrase!\p“Let's trade!”\pI almost don't need to explain this\nphrase! Let's translate it!\p“Koukan shiyou yo!“\nKo-o-ka-n shee-yo-o yo!\pWhat is important is to have a glint in\nyour eye, like you're really excited!\pIf you communicate your excitement,\nI'm sure you can make a good trade!\pSo that's it for today!\nSee you, everyone! JA NE!$"
gBwText_462_126:
	.string "Toru: YA, MINNA!\pIn today's “KOUKAN TALK,“\nI'm going to introduce something\lthat's often said to me.\p“You're kidding!”\pThere is often a lot of shocking\nnews in my circle of friends.\pWhen I said I saw a bright\nred {STR_VAR_3},\lthis is what they said to me!\p“Jodan deshou!“\nJo-da-n de-sho-o!\pYou're kidding?!\nI'm serious!\pI saw a very angry\n{STR_VAR_3}, and its face\lwas bright red!\l...Man, I was scared!\pSo that's all for today!\nMATA KONDO, everyone!$"
gBwText_462_127:
	.string "Toru: MINNA, KONNICHIWA!\nIn today's “KOUKAN TALK,“\pwe're going to teach you an aggressive\nway to proclaim your future victory!\p“I'm going to win!”\p“Katsu zo!“\nKa-tsu zo!\pWhat is important is to emphasize the\n“zo!” Be aggressive\land show where you stand!\pFor example, saying it through clenched\nteeth would be really cool.\pYou might not even have to battle! Just\ndeclare victory like that, and your\lopponent might get scared and run\laway!\pSo that's it for today!\nLet's meet again! JA NE!$"
gBwText_462_128:
	.string "Toru: KONNICHI-HELLO!\pIt's “KOUKAN TALK,“ which gives\nyou great tips for talking in Japanese!\pToday's phrase is this!\n“What was that about!?”\pThis is something you spout out\nwithout thinking when something\lunexpected happens!\pThis is how you say it in Japanese!\n“Nandattendayo!“\pNa-n-da te-n-da-yo!\nThe point is your expression.\pIf you say this while making an\nexpression that says, “What?” II YO!\pWell, that's it for today!\pPlease look forward to next week's\ninstallment!\pMATA RAISHU!$"
gBwText_462_129:
	.string "Toru: Hello, everyone!\pIn today's “KOUKAN TALK,“\nwe will teach you the question to\lend all questions!\p“What's your hobby?”\pUse it with people you've just met! Use\nit with people you've known forever!\pIn Japanese, you say this:\n“Shumi nani?“\lShu-mee nah-nee?\pThat should get the conversation\ngoing!\pWell, that's it for today!\nPlease watch again!\lMATA KONDO!$"
gBwText_462_130:
	.string "Host: Today, on “Eyes on Unova,“ we will\nintroduce you to:\pA couple of genius musicians who live in\nan exceptionally high part of Accumula\lTown!\pHello! Why are you living in such a\nhigh-up place?\pWoman: I wanted to live in a house where\nI could make music without bothering\lanyone, but I also wanted to live close\lto the city and all its people.\pMan: Also, I thought it would be nice if\nour music could ride the wind...\pMinccino: Chip kwip!\pHost: ...So that's the word!\pIf you hear beautiful music carried on\nthe breeze, it feels magical, doesn't\lit?\pAnd this concludes our interview\nfrom Accumula Town.$"
gBwText_462_131:
	.string "Host: Today, on “Eyes on Unova,“ we will\nintroduce you to:\pA talented Pokémon massage therapist\nwho lives in Castelia City!\pHello! So what got you interested in\nPokémon massage therapy?\pWoman: At first, I wanted to be a\nmassage therapist for people, but one\lday I didn't have any human clients, so\lI decided to practice on a Pokémon.\pIt was so happy and so cute afterward!\nSo I decided to switch my practice to\lPokémon massage exclusively.\pHost: Wow, is that so? That means you\ncan do massage for people too, right?!\pIf you don't mind, my neck has been\nkilling me...\p...Oh, well, that's...\nerk... Maybe you're out of practice...\low ow OW! OK, that's enough, thanks!\pThat was...ow...\nour report from Castelia City.$"
gBwText_462_132:
	.string "Host: Today, on “Eyes on Unova,“ we will\nintroduce you to:\pThis wonderful lady who lives right here\nin Driftveil City!\pHello! You are the lady who is famous\nfor being obsessed with TMs, right?\pWoman: That's right. Are you familiar\nwith a move called Spite?\pHost: Um... I've heard of it...\pWoman: I will not speak to you unless\nyou bring me a Pokémon that knows\lSpite!\pHost: Well, I think we can confirm that\nyou're every bit as eccentric\las people say!\pAnd that was our report\nfrom Driftveil City.$"
gBwText_462_133:
	.string "Host: Today, on “Eyes on Unova,“ we will\nintroduce you to:\pA family in Mistralton City that has a\nspecial way with Pokémon moves!\pHello! Is it true that you can make\nPokémon forget and remember moves?\pOlder man: Sure thing! Which move would\nyou like to forget?\pHost: No, wait!\n...Aaaagh!\p...\n...Huh? I forgot how to broadcast...\pGirl: And I'll make you remember\nit again! OK, go!\pHost: Oh! That's right...\nAnd that's our report from\lMistralton City!$"
gBwText_462_134:
	.string "Host: Today, on “Eyes on Unova,“ we will\nintroduce you to:\pA woman in Icirrus City who studies the\nbonds between Trainers and Pokémon!\pHello! Now, why are you so interested in\nthe bonds between people and Pokémon?\pWoman: Don't you feel nice when you see\npeople and Pokémon getting along well?\pI get to see so much of that in my job.\nI love it!\pHost: Is that so? Can you also read\nhow well people are getting along with\leach other?\pWoman: That's right. Take you and me,\nfor example...\p...Nope, nothing.\pHost: And that was our report\nfrom Icirrus City.$"
gBwText_462_135:
	.string "Host: Today, on “Eyes on Unova,“ we will\nintroduce you to:\pAn older man from Opelucid City who\nloves musicals!\pHello! I've heard that you hand out\nMusical Props every day!\pMan: Indubitably! ? C'est vrai! ?\pHost: Oh dear. There's really no need\nto sing about it, sir...\pMan: ? Beeee-caaaause ? bee-cause ?...\pHost: OK, OK, thank you very much!\nThat was our report from\lOpelucid City!$"
gBwText_462_136:
	.string "Host: Today, on “Eyes on Unova,“ we will\nintroduce you to:\pA little Minccino who lives the slow,\nrelaxed life in Lacunosa Town!\pMinccino: Gahoohoo!\pHost: Oh, you're so cute!\nHow can you be so cute?!\pMinccino: Gahooo.\pHost: Really? That sounds pretty tough.\pMinccino: Gahoo...hoo.\pHost: Oh, you're sooo cute! But I'm\nsorry... I have to admit I don't\lunderstand a thing you're saying!\pWell, that was our report from\nLacunosa Town!\pMinccino: Gahoo!$"
gBwText_462_137:
	.string "Host: Today, on “Eyes on Unova,“ we will\nintroduce you to:\pThe famous fisherman of Village Bridge!\pHi there! I've heard you're always\nlooking for other people who love\lfishing!\pFamous Fisherman: That's right! I wanna\nget more people in the Hip Waders!\pGet 'em to join up and have a good\ntime fishing with me!\pHost: But don't most people prefer\nfishing as a solitary sport?\pFamous Fisherman: Now, that ain't true!\nTwo are better than one!\lFour are better than two!\lFour are better than four!\lWait, I got confused...\pNever mind. Hey, lady! How about you\njoin the club? You can be a Hip Wader,\ltoo!\pHost: OK, thank you! Well, that was our\nreport from Village Bridge!$"
gBwText_462_138:
	.string "Tralala, tralala... ?\pThe most sparkling move used in\ntoday's Musical was...\pA lovely spinning somersault! Yes!\pI'm sure you wouldn't think Pokémon\ncould do somersaults, but they can!\pThey spin like pinwheels on the stage!\nIt's total freedom!\pUp, down, left, right... It's like gravity\ndoesn't even matter!\lYeah, yeah, yeah, freedom!\pHaaarmony! ? Daaance! ? Muuusical! ?\pHost: And that concludes our\nlive coverage.$"
gBwText_462_139:
	.string "Host: Today, on “Eyes on Unova,“ we will\nintroduce you to:\pOne of the rich and fabulous folks of\nUndella Town!\pHello! Gosh, this is a huuuge manor,\nisn't it?\pMan: Wow, that's rich. But you're on the\nmoney! Want to check out my collection?\lGive me your two cents?\pHost: Um... Sure! Wow, this is amazing.\nWhat kinds of things do you collect?\pMan: Well, I've got a cash--I mean,\na cache--of really rare stuff.\lDough what I mean?\pHost: Oh, I'm sorry, do you have a cold?\nBut I do know what you mean. Your\lcollection is lovely, thank you!\pThat's our report from Undella Town!$"
gBwText_462_140:
	.string "Host: Welcome to “PokéQuiz,“ where we\nquiz kids who love Pokémon, but don't\llike language lessons, on the Japanese\lnames of Pokémon!\pToday's Pokémon is Pikachu!\nWhat is it called in Japanese?\pNo hint is necessary this time, because\nit's international!\pOK, panelists, your answers, please?\pQuil: Oh! It's Electchu!\pIll: I know! It's Pikanezumi!\pZill: Ah! It's Pikapika!\pHost: Oh, too bad! The correct answer is\nPikachu! Just like in English!\pAs a matter of fact, wherever you go in\nthe world, Pikachu is Pikachu!\pOK then, see you next week!\nFarewell!$"
gBwText_462_141:
	.string "Host: Welcome to “PokéQuiz,“ where we\nquiz kids who love Pokémon, but don't\llike language lessons, on the Japanese\lnames of Pokémon!\pToday's Pokémon is Hoothoot!\nWhat is it called in Japanese?\pHere's a big hint! In Japanese, the\nsound it makes is “hoo”!\pOK, you three, start from\nthere!\pQuill: Oh! It's Hoo!\pIll: I know! It's Hoohoo!\pZill: Oh yeah! It's Hooareyou!\pHost: Oh, Ill was so close! The correct\nanswer is Hoho! Ho-o ho-o!\pI'll bet you learned a lot!\pWell then, see you next week!\nFarewell!$"
gBwText_462_142:
	.string "Host: Welcome to “PokéQuiz,“ where we\nquiz kids who love Pokémon, but don't\llike language lessons, on the Japanese\lnames of Pokémon!\pToday's Pokémon is Lickitung!\nWhat is it called in Japanese?\pThe hint is, its long tongue is called\na “bero!”\pOK, go to work, my energetic\nthree-person team!\pQuill: Oh, it's Lickitung!\pIll: I know! It's Berong!\pZill: Oh yeah, it's Berlin!\pHost: Ooh! Too bad!\pThe correct answer is Beroringa!\nBe-ro-ri-n-ga!\pBerori is the sound of licking in\nJapanese!\pIt's an easy-to-understand name\nthat emphasizes the looong\ltongue it is known for!\pOK, see you later!\nFarewell!$"
gBwText_462_143:
	.string "Host: Welcome to “PokéQuiz,“ where we\nquiz kids who love Pokémon, but don't\llike language lessons, on the Japanese\lnames of Pokémon!\pToday's Pokémon is Eevee!\nWhat is it called in Japanese?\pOK, you over there!\pQuill: Oh! It's Eevee!\pIll: I know! It's Eve!\pZill: Oh yeah! It's Eievui!\pHost: Oh! I can't believe it!\nThat's correct!\pThe answer is Eievui! Ee-vee!\nCongratulations!\pThe person with the correct\nanswer wins an Eevee doll!\p...Well then, see you next week!\nFarewell!$"
gBwText_462_144:
	.string "Host: Welcome to “PokéQuiz,“ where we\nquiz kids who love Pokémon, but don't\llike language lessons, on the Japanese\lnames of Pokémon!\pToday's Pokémon is Turtwig!\nWhat is it called in Japanese?\pOK, you three sleepy-looking\nkids over there!\pQuill: Is it Turtwig?\pIll: Is it Torunae?\pZill: Is it Tornado?\pHost: Oh, sorry. The correct answer\nis Naetle!\p“Nae” means seedling in Japanese, and\nTurtwig has a seedling growing out of\lits head! Did you learn something?\pWell then, see you next week!\nFarewell!$"
gBwText_462_145:
	.string "Host: Welcome to “PokéQuiz,“ where we\nquiz kids who love Pokémon, but don't\llike language lessons, on the Japanese\lnames of Pokémon!\pToday's Pokémon is Squirtle!\nWhat is Squirtle in Japanese?\lOK, you over there!\pQuill: Oh! It's Squirtle!\pIll: I know! It's Turzen!\pZill: Oh yeah! It's Zenzen!\pHost: So sorry!\pThe answer is Zenigame!\nZeh-nee-ga-me!\p“Zeni” is an old-fashioned word\nfor money.\pSquirtle's shells look like old coins,\nso that's how they got their name!\lYou can't use them as coins, though.\pOK, see you next week!\nFarewell!$"
gBwText_462_146:
	.string "Host: Welcome to “PokéQuiz,“ where we\nquiz kids who love Pokémon, but don't\llike language lessons, on the Japanese\lnames of Pokémon!\pToday's Pokémon is Geodude!\nOK, what is it called in Japanese?\pWhat do you think, you kids who\nlook like you enjoy learning?\pQuill: Oh! It's Geodude!\pIll: I know! It's Geometery!\pZill: Oh yeah! It's Geometeric!\pHost: The correct answer's\nIshitsubute! I-shee-tsu-bu-te!\p“Ishi” means rock, and\n“tsubute“ is like a throwing stone.\pDon't try to throw a Geodude, though,\nbecause you will probably get hurt!\pOK, see you next week!\nFarewell!$"
gBwText_462_147:
	.string "Host: Welcome to “PokéQuiz,“ where we\nquiz kids who love Pokémon, but don't\llike language lessons, on the Japanese\lnames of Pokémon!\pToday's Pokémon is Wailord!\nOK, what is it called in Japanese?\pOK, you three kids there with\nthe confident expressions!\pQuill: Oh! It's Wailord!\pIll: I know! It's Ohwhale!\pZill: Oh yeah! It's Ohwell!\pHost: Oh! That's incorrect!\nThe correct answer is Whaloh!\lIt's pronounced: ho-e-ru-o-o!\p“Hoeru” means “wail,“ and the\n“oh” at the end means “king.“\pMaybe it's sad and lonely at the top!\nHas a very noble sound to it, doesn't\lit?\pOK, see you next week!$"
gBwText_462_148:
	.string "Host: Welcome to “PokéQuiz,“ where we\nquiz kids who love Pokémon, but don't\llike language lessons, on the Japanese\lnames of Pokémon!\pToday's Pokémon is Machop!\nWhat is it called in Japanese?\pThe hint is, “riki” means strength\nin Japanese.\pOK, you three over there!\nYour answers please!\pQuill: Oh! It's Machop!\pIll: I know! It's Mabrarian!\pZill: Oh yeah! It's Chopchop!\pHost: Sorry, that's incorrect!\pThe correct answer is Wanriky!\nWa-n-ri-kee!\p“Wan“ means “arm,” and\n“riki“ means “strength.”\lIt's very easy to understand!\pWell then, everyone,\nfarewell! Mah-mah-machooo!$"
gBwText_462_149:
	.string "Host: Welcome to “PokéQuiz,“ where we\nquiz kids who love Pokémon, but don't\llike language lessons, on the Japanese\lnames of Pokémon!\pToday's Pokémon is Beautifly!\nWhat is it called in Japanese?\lOK, you three over there!\pQuill: Oh! It's Beautifly!\pIll: I know! It's Flybeauti!\pZill: Oh yeah! It's Flyfly!\pHost: Nope, the correct answer is\nAgehunt! A-ge-ha-n-to!\pThe “hunt” part makes it sound\nferocious for such a pretty Pokémon.\pOK, see you next week!\nFarewell!$"
gBwText_462_150:
	.string "Narrator: It's time for “Your Pokémon“!\pOn today's “Your Pokémon,” we will\nintroduce an energetic little one.\pThe Pokémon of this new Trainer who\nis running around Route 2 energetically\lis the Lillipup called Ran!\pIts Trainer heads for Route 2 with Ran\nevery day.\pRan has never lost a battle there, and\nit refuses to lose to any Pokémon!\pIt's running around the tall grass\nwith its owner today as well!\pThat was Ran, who is very energetic,\nbut not as much as my li'l Lillipup!\pOn the next “Your Pokémon,“\nwe will introduce another fantastic\lPokémon...who is great, but not\lquite as great as mine!$"
gBwText_462_151:
	.string "Narrator: It's “Your Pokémon“!\pOn today's “Your Pokémon,” we will\nintroduce a helpful little one!\pIn a two-story home in Striaton City,\nthe Patrat called Peeps\llives with its Trainer.\pIts Trainer is also a Pokémon Breeder\nwho is raising many Pokémon!\pAnd when its Trainer is really busy,\nPeeps lends a hand...or a paw! It plays\lwith all the other Pokémon to give them\lsome exercise and sometimes even gets\lthem to settle down for the night.\pToday, Peeps has started a lively game\nof tag with some of the other Pokémon\lits Trainer is taking care of.\pThey'll sleep well tonight after\nall that running!\pThat was the Patrat Peeps, who is\nhelpful, but not as much as my Patrat.\pOn the next “Your Pokémon,“ we will\nmeet another Pokémon who works hard,\lbut not as hard as mine!$"
gBwText_462_152:
	.string "Narrator: It's “Your Pokémon“!\pOn today's “Your Pokémon,” we will\nintroduce a hard-working little one!\pIn Nacrene City's old warehouses, the\nPurrloin Meg lives with its Trainer.\pMeg's Trainer runs a store, and every\nmorning, Meg goes to work with her.\pAt the store, Meg is its Trainer's\npartner! It sits outside as a mascot\land draws customers into the store.\pToday, it's even carrying a sign for the\nstore to attract even more customers!\pThat was the Purrloin Meg, who works\nhard, but not as hard as my Purrloin.\pOn the next “Your Pokémon,“ we will\nintroduce a little Pokémon with\la lot of fighting spirit, but not as much\las mine!$"
gBwText_462_153:
	.string "Narrator: It's “Your Pokémon“!\pOn today's “Your Pokémon,” we will\nintroduce a little one with a great\lfighting spirit!\pIn a Castelia City office building,\na Darumaka named Gance is having\la Pokémon battle.\pIts Trainer is a Clerk ? who works in\nthe building.\pThis company takes Pokémon battles\nvery seriously. In fact, work schedules,\lmeeting agendas, and other important\lmatters are all decided by battles!\pAnd so its Trainer won't have to work\non weekends or do really boring jobs,\lGance does its very best in every\lbattle.\pThe Darumaka Gance is a Pokémon\nwith fighting spirit, but not as much as\lmy Darumaka!\pOn the next “Your Pokémon,“ we will\nintroduce a Pokémon that stands out,\lbut not as much as mine!$"
gBwText_462_154:
	.string "Narrator: It's “Your Pokémon“!\pOn today's “Your Pokémon,” we will\nintroduce a little one that stands out!\pIt's waiting in the wings in the Nimbasa\nCity Musical for its cue to go on stage.\lThis Minccino is named Julie!\pJulie and its Trainer have put so much\neffort into training for the Musical.\lThey've worked really hard!\pAnd for Julie, the goal every day is\nto be the one that gets the most time\lin the spotlight!\pJulie and its Trainer have a real fire in\ntheir hearts when it comes to\lperforming!\pThat was the Minccino Julie, who stands\nout, just not as much as my Minccino.\pOn the next “Your Pokémon,“ we will\nintroduce a Pokémon that's really good\lat napping, but not as good as mine!$"
gBwText_462_155:
	.string "Narrator: It's “Your Pokémon“!\pOn today's “Your Pokémon,” we will\nintroduce a very relaxed little one!\pIn a small house in Driftveil City, the\nCubchoo named Kodie lives\lwith its Trainer.\pKodie's Trainer is a Worker in the\nCold Storage.\pKodie tags along to work and takes a\nnap right there in the Cold Storage.\pEven when it's cold enough that its\nTrainer's teeth are chattering, Kodie\lnaps away in perfect comfort!\pThat was Kodie, who's very relaxed, but\nnot as relaxed as my Cubchoo!\pOn the next “Your Pokémon,“ we will\nintroduce a Pokémon that is patient,\lbut not as patient as mine!$"
gBwText_462_156:
	.string "Narrator: It's “Your Pokémon“!\pOn today's “Your Pokémon,” we will\nintroduce a very patient little one!\pIn Mistralton City, a Crustle called\nAmine spends a lot of time at the\lCargo Plane Center.\pYou see, Amine's Trainer is a Pilot! He\noften flies overseas for work, and\lAmine doesn't always know when he will\lreturn.\pSo Amine waits at the Cargo Plane\nCenter and watches the sky for its\lTrainer's plane.\pThat was the Crustle Amine,\nwhich is patient, but not as patient\las my Crustle.\pOn the next “Your Pokémon,“ we will\nintroduce a Pokémon that is an\lexcellent judge, but not as good as\lmine!$"
gBwText_462_157:
	.string "Narrator: It's “Your Pokémon“!\pOn today's “Your Pokémon,” we will\nintroduce a little one with\lexcellent judgment.\pIn a stone home in Icirrus City, the\nSwoobat named Amour lives\lwith its family.\pWhen there is an argument in the family,\nthey ask Amour to settle it!\pShould we go to the mountain or stream?\nShould dinner be vegetables or Berries?\pAmour listens to everyone's side\nand makes a careful judgment.\pThat was the Swoobat Amour, who has\nexcellent judgment skills, but not as\lgood as my Swoobat's!\pOn the next “Your Pokémon,“ we will\nintroduce a Pokémon that eats a lot,\lbut not as much as mine!$"
gBwText_462_158:
	.string "Narrator: It's “Your Pokémon“!\pOn today's “Your Pokémon,” we will\nintroduce a little one that loves to\leat!\pNear the gate of Opelucid City, the\nZweilous Chow lives with its Trainer.\pBoth Chow and its Trainer really love to\neat! Anything you serve them, they'll\lgobble it right up. They even compete\lagainst each other in eating contests.\pBack when Chow was a Deino, its Trainer\ncould eat faster...but now that Chow\lhas evolved into a Zweilous, it has an\lextra mouth, so that's a big advantage!\pIt's built up quite a winning streak\nwith its two hungry hungry heads.\pThat was the Zweilous, Chow, who\neats a lot, but not as much\las my Zweilous.\pOn the next “Your Pokémon,“ we will\nintroduce a Pokémon that is amazing...\lbut, of course, not as amazing as mine!$"
gBwText_462_159:
	.string "Narrator: It's “Your Pokémon“!\pOn today's “Your Pokémon,” we will\nintroduce an amazing little one!\pDeep in Victory Road, the Throh Heishi\nis fighting with its Trainer, a Black\lBelt. But don't worry, they're just\ltraining!\pThe Trainer beat Heishi in a judo match\nthe first time they met. That's how\lthey became friends.\pAfter a long, hard journey, they've\nfinally arrived at Victory Road.\pHeishi's Trainer wants to become\nChampion, of course...and Heishi's dream\lis to beat the Champion in a judo match!\pThat was the Throh Heishi,\nwho is amazing, but not as amazing\las my Throh.\pOn the next “Your Pokémon,“ we will\nintroduce a Pokémon that is energetic,\lbut not as energetic as mine!$"
gBwText_462_160:
	.string "...\n...\p...\n...Zzt.$"
gBwText_462_161:
	.string "So this is today's recommended item:\na darling Poké Doll!\pJust touch it for a second!\nIsn't it so soft? That's right!\pIt's made from Unova's\nfinest-grade cotton!\pIt feels like touching a cloud,\nand it's as light as a feather!\pAnd it looks so real! Like it could leap\ninto battle at any second...\pBut relax! If you just put this Poké\nDoll down, you can escape for sure!\pThis highest-quality Poké Doll\nis available for only...\pBut wait, there's more! If you call\nright now, we'll throw in a Potion, too.\lAnd all for just $28,000,000!\pOperators are standing by!$"
gBwText_462_162:
	.string "So this is today's recommended item!\pAt first glance, it looks just like an\nordinary, convenient Repel!\pBut take a whiff! Look!\nIsn't it an elegant fragrance?\pJust wearing this sophisticated\naroma will draw the eyes of Trainers\lworldwide straight to you!\pThis is a special floral Repel!\pAnd for a limited time, it is available\nas part of a Max Repel deal for an\lunbelievable $3,500,000!\lCall NOW!$"
gBwText_462_163:
	.string "So this is today's recommended item!\pAt first glance, it looks like nothing\nmore than your handy traveling\lcompanion, the Potion! But just taste\lit!\pSuch a smooth flavor! That's right!\nThis exquisite Potion was made by\lUnova's finest pastry chef.\pIt makes you feel good inside and out!\pAnd when you order this amazingly\ndelicious chef's-special Potion, we'll\lthrow in a fantastic regular Potion,\ltoo!\pAll for an amaaazing $3,000,000!\nCall NOW!$"
gBwText_462_164:
	.string "So this is today's recommended item!\pAt first glance it looks like an\nordinary Poké Ball!\pBut look! It has a captivating beauty!\pThat's right! This designer Poké Ball\nwas made with exacting detail by a\lfirst-class jeweler!\pYou wouldn't want to catch just any\nPokémon in this gorgeous Ball. Besides,\lthe ornamentation would break off if\lyou threw it!\pBut just by carrying this around, you\nwill become dramatically more\lfashionable! It's quite a statement!\pThis designer Poké Ball made by a top\njeweler is available now, in a set with a\lregular Poké Ball for catching,\lfor a mere $20,000,000!\lCall NOW!$"
gBwText_462_165:
	.string "So this is today's recommended item!\pAt first glance, it looks like an\nordinary Escape Rope!\pBut, look closer! Check out this knot!\pThat's right! This rope was expertly\nknotted by a veteran sailor.\pNow you won't have to worry about the\nrope getting tangled up in your bag!\pNo matter how hard you pull,\nyou'll never undo the knot!\pAn Escape Rope tied in an expert\nknot by a veteran craftsman!\pFor a limited time, you can get it in a\nset with a regular old Escape Rope for a\lfantastic $3,000,000! Call NOW!$"
gBwText_462_166:
	.string "“Unova News“: Next, we have an\ninterview with Ms. A, who was stranded\lon a snowy mountain for three days\lbefore she was found in a town in the\lfoothills.\pMs. A: It was definitely Cubchoo!\pJust when I was out of strength\nand about to fall asleep,\lI saw it!\pIt was the shadow of something\nliving, and the next day I woke up\lin this town in the foothills.\pThe people in this town say I got\nhere by myself, but it was definitely\lbecause of Cubchoo!\pI'm sure it saved me!\p“Unova News”: This concludes the\ninterview with Ms. A.$"
gBwText_462_167:
	.string "“Unova News“: Next up, a column in\nGear Station is said to have\lmoved on its own.\pWe have an interview with\nMr. B, the only witness.\pMr. B: Yup, I done seen it!\pAll of tha sudden I done heard\na noise like klink klink klink, and then...\lrrrwrrrwrrrwrrrBOOM!\lAnd the column spun right 'round!\pThen, when I heard that klink-klinkin'\nagain and looked up, something that\llooked kinda like a little gear went\la-flyin' away.\pI'm shore it was that little\nfeller's doin'.\pIt was one of them there Pokey-mon.\nShore was.\p“Unova News”: That concludes our\ninterview with Mr. B.$"
gBwText_462_168:
	.string "“Unova News“: This is so exciting! We're\nspeaking to a woman who actually saw\la living ice-cream cone!\pMs. C: I wanted a Casteliacone no matter\nwhat, and I came all the way in from the\lcountryside to get one.\pThen, I waited in a looong line\nand finally bought the ice cream.\pWhen I was just about to take a nibble,\nthe ice cream moved!\pIt startled me, so I dropped it, and it\nran away!\lCould that have been a Pokémon?\p“Unova News”: That concludes our\ninterview with Ms. C.$"
gBwText_462_169:
	.string "“Unova News“: Next up, we have news of\na Pokémon that can see the future.\pMs. D: I was elegantly strolling\nalong the beach.\pThen I saw a Pokémon off in the\ndistance. It was looking intently in my\ldirection for some reason.\pIt just sat there staring, so at first,\nI thought it was looking at me, but...\pIt suddenly pointed to the ocean\nand disappeared!\pI wanted to know what it was pointing\nat, so I walked toward the ocean...\pAnd then! A big boulder fell down from\nthe cliff above!\pRight where I had just been standing!\pI'm sure that Pokémon can\nsee the future!\lThere's no doubt about it!\pIt protected the future of a\nbeautiful lady like me.\p“Unova News”: ...Uh-huh. This concludes\nthe report on Ms. D.$"
	.align 2
	.global gBwTextTable_462
