gBwText_471_0:
	.string "Welcome to the Global Terminal!$"
gBwText_471_1:
	.string "Would you like to use\nNintendo Wi-Fi Connection?$"
gBwText_471_2:
	.string "Please do visit again.$"
gBwText_471_3:
	.string "$"
gBwText_471_4:
	.string "Right this way, please.$"
gBwText_471_5:
	.string "In the Global Terminal, you can battle\nor trade Pokémon with Pokémon fans\lfrom around the world by connecting to\lNintendo Wi-Fi Connection.\pFor details, please listen to the\nexplanation at each facility.$"
gBwText_471_6:
	.string "Sorry, we're getting things ready.\nPlease come back later.$"
gBwText_471_7:
	.string "You have at least one Pokémon\nthat can't be taken in.$"
gBwText_471_8:
	.string "Communication error.$"
gBwText_471_9:
	.string "Random Matchup$"
gBwText_471_10:
	.string "Global Trade$"
gBwText_471_11:
	.string "Musical Photos$"
gBwText_471_12:
	.string "Battle Videos$"
gBwText_471_13:
	.string "Info$"
gBwText_471_14:
	.string "Cancel$"
gBwText_471_15:
	.string "Would you like to make a Global Trade?$"
gBwText_471_16:
	.string "You may trade Pokémon with other\nPokémon fans from around the world\lwith Global Trade.\pGlobal Trade has two forms: GTS and\nGTS Negotiations.\pPlease be careful, because each has a\ndifferent way of trading.$"
gBwText_471_17:
	.string "GTS$"
gBwText_471_18:
	.string "GTS Negotiations$"
gBwText_471_19:
	.string "Info$"
gBwText_471_20:
	.string "Back$"
gBwText_471_21:
	.string "Would you like to make a GTS trade?$"
gBwText_471_22:
	.string "Trade$"
gBwText_471_23:
	.string "Info$"
gBwText_471_24:
	.string "Back$"
gBwText_471_25:
	.string "You may trade Pokémon in two ways when\nusing GTS.\pYou may offer a Pokémon for trade\nor search among offered Pokémon.$"
gBwText_471_26:
	.string "Should I describe things in\ngreater detail?$"
gBwText_471_27:
	.string "You will be asked to put up the\nPokémon you are offering to trade.\pAt that time, you will be asked what\nPokémon you would like in return.\pIf another player offers your desired\nPokémon in return for your offered\lPokémon, the trade will go through.$"
gBwText_471_28:
	.string "You may search among the Pokémon\nthat are offered by other Trainers.\pThey will all identify what Pokémon\ntheir Trainers want back in return.\pIf you find one that you want, you\nmust provide us with the kind of\lPokémon wanted in return.$"
gBwText_471_29:
	.string "Offer Pokémon?$"
gBwText_471_30:
	.string "Seek Pokémon?$"
gBwText_471_31:
	.string "Understood$"
gBwText_471_32:
	.string "Would you like to start\nPokémon GTS Negotiations?$"
gBwText_471_33:
	.string "Start Negotiations$"
gBwText_471_34:
	.string "Info$"
gBwText_471_35:
	.string "Back$"
gBwText_471_36:
	.string "In GTS Negotiations, you set the\ntrading conditions based on what kinds\lof Pokémon you'd like to trade.\pIf you find a person with matching\nconditions, you may proceed to a\lNegotiation Trade with that person.\pIn order to trade, you need to have two\nor more Pokémon in your party.$"
gBwText_471_37:
	.string "Should I describe things in\ngreater detail?$"
gBwText_471_38:
	.string "In a Negotiation Trade, each person\noffers three Pokémon to trade.\pThen, each person will choose one of\nthe other person's three Pokémon.$"
gBwText_471_39:
	.string "You can set three conditions in a\nNegotiation Trade: the level of Pokémon\lto trade, the Pokémon you want to\lreceive, and the Pokémon up for offer.\pYou may trade with a person whose\nconditions match yours, or choose\lTrade Rendezvous to try another trade\lwith a previous trading partner.$"
gBwText_471_40:
	.string "Negotiation Trade?$"
gBwText_471_41:
	.string "Trading Conditions?$"
gBwText_471_42:
	.string "Understood$"
gBwText_471_43:
	.string "Would you like to view or upload\nBattle Videos?$"
gBwText_471_44:
	.string "With Battle Videos, you may post a\nBattle Video you took with your\lVs. Recorder or view Battle Videos from\lother Trainers.\pYou may search the Battle Videos by\nPokémon, battle facility, ranking, etc.\pThe Battle Video you post will be\nassigned a 12-digit code.\pYour friends may view your Battle Video\nby entering this 12-digit code here.$"
gBwText_471_45:
	.string "View or upload$"
gBwText_471_46:
	.string "Info$"
gBwText_471_47:
	.string "Back$"
gBwText_471_48:
	.string "Would you like to view or upload\nMusical Photos?$"
gBwText_471_49:
	.string "With Musical Photos, you may post a\nphoto you took at the Pokémon Musical\lin Nimbasa City by using the Vs.\lRecorder.\pYou may also view photos taken by other\npeople, sorted by the Pokémon you like.$"
gBwText_471_50:
	.string "View or upload$"
gBwText_471_51:
	.string "Info$"
gBwText_471_52:
	.string "Back$"
gBwText_471_53:
	.string "Would you like to take the\nRandom Matchup challenge?$"
gBwText_471_54:
	.string "Challenge$"
gBwText_471_55:
	.string "Info$"
gBwText_471_56:
	.string "Back$"
gBwText_471_57:
	.string "A Random Matchup is a battle with other\nPokémon fans from around the world.\pThere are five kinds of Random\nMatchups: Single, Double, Triple,\lRotation, and Launcher.\pAlso, Random Matchups have two modes:\nFree mode and Rating mode.\pIn Free mode, everyone can participate\nin battles freely.\pIn Rating mode, you may participate in\nbattles after you set Game Sync,\laccess the Pokémon Global Link website\lwith your computer, and register your\lGame Sync ID.\phttp://www.pokemon-gl.com/\n(Pokémon Global Link)$"
gBwText_471_58:
	.string "Would you like to know more details?$"
gBwText_471_59:
	.string "Free Mode$"
gBwText_471_60:
	.string "Rating Mode$"
gBwText_471_61:
	.string "Special Rules$"
gBwText_471_62:
	.string "Understood$"
gBwText_471_63:
	.string "Free mode is for casual battles against\nother Pokémon fans around the world.\pFeel free to challenge it!$"
gBwText_471_64:
	.string "Rating mode is recommended for those\nwho want to master battles.\pWhen communication is established, you\nare likely to battle against a person\lwith a similar Rating.\pYour Rating starts at 1500. When you\nwin, it goes up. When you lose, it goes\ldown.\pSo the higher your Rating is, the\nstronger you are as a Trainer!\pThere's one thing you should be careful\nabout in Rating mode.\pYour record and Rating will be erased if\nyou connect to Nintendo Wi-Fi\lConnection with a different DS System.\pSo please be careful if you switch!$"
gBwText_471_65:
	.string "There are several special rules\nfor Random Matchups.\pAny Pokémon higher than Lv. 50 will be\nset to that level for the battle.\pPokémon nicknames won't be used.\pYou have a limited time to choose\nPokémon for a battle and to give orders\lto your Pokémon during the battle.\pDon't exceed the time limit,\nor your Pokémon and its moves\lwill be chosen for you!\pThere's also a time limit on the battle.\pThe winner will be determined when time\nruns out, even if both sides still have\lPokémon standing.$"
gBwText_471_66:
	.string "Which Battle would you like\nto choose?$"
gBwText_471_67:
	.string "Single Battle$"
gBwText_471_68:
	.string "Double Battle$"
gBwText_471_69:
	.string "Triple Battle$"
gBwText_471_70:
	.string "Rotation Battle$"
gBwText_471_71:
	.string "Launcher Battle$"
gBwText_471_72:
	.string "Back$"
gBwText_471_73:
	.string "Would you like to take the\nSingle Battle challenge?$"
gBwText_471_74:
	.string "Would you like to take the \nDouble Battle Challenge?$"
gBwText_471_75:
	.string "Would you like to take the \nTriple Battle Challenge?$"
gBwText_471_76:
	.string "Would you like to take the \nRotation Battle Challenge?$"
gBwText_471_77:
	.string "Would you like to take the \nLauncher Battle Challenge?$"
gBwText_471_78:
	.string "Confirm$"
gBwText_471_79:
	.string "Rules$"
gBwText_471_80:
	.string "Back$"
gBwText_471_81:
	.string "For a Single Battle, you need to have\nthree to six Pokémon.\pBefore a battle, you and your opponent\nshow your Pokémon to each other,\lthen choose three Pokémon and battle.\pYou may not have duplicate Pokémon\nor held items.\pAlso, you can't take special Pokémon\nor Eggs into battle.$"
gBwText_471_82:
	.string "For a Double Battle, you need to have\nfour to six Pokémon.\pBefore a battle, you and your opponent\nshow your Pokémon to each other,\lthen choose four Pokémon and battle.\pYou may not have duplicate Pokémon\nor held items.\pAlso, you can't take special Pokémon\nor Eggs into battle.$"
gBwText_471_83:
	.string "For a Triple Battle, you need to have\nsix Pokémon.\pBefore a battle, you and your opponent\nshow your Pokémon to each other,\lthen decide their order and battle.\pYou may not have duplicate Pokémon\nor held items.\pAlso, you can't take special Pokémon\nor Eggs into battle.$"
gBwText_471_84:
	.string "In a Rotation Battle, you need to have\nfour to six Pokémon.\pBefore a battle, you and your opponent\nshow your Pokémon to each other,\lthen choose four Pokémon and battle.\pYou may not have duplicate Pokémon\nor held items.\pAlso, you can't take special Pokémon\nor Eggs into battle.$"
gBwText_471_85:
	.string "In a Launcher Battle, you have a Triple\nBattle with your Wonder Launcher. You\lneed to have six Pokémon.\pBefore a battle, you and your opponent\nshow your Pokémon to each other,\lthen decide their order and battle.\pYou may not have duplicate Pokémon\nor held items.\pAlso, you can't take special Pokémon\nor Eggs into battle.$"
gBwText_471_86:
	.string "$"
gBwText_471_87:
	.string "$"
gBwText_471_88:
	.string "$"
gBwText_471_89:
	.string "$"
gBwText_471_90:
	.string "$"
gBwText_471_91:
	.string "$"
gBwText_471_92:
	.string "$"
gBwText_471_93:
	.string "$"
gBwText_471_94:
	.string "Uh-oh!\pI'm sorry, but your party and all your\nPC Boxes are full.\pTo use the GTS, you must have\nroom in your party or in a PC Box.$"
gBwText_471_95:
	.string "Uh-oh!\pYou need at least two Pokémon in your\nparty to use the GTS.$"
gBwText_471_96:
	.string "Uh-oh!\pYou need at least two Pokémon in your\nparty to use GTS Negotiations.$"
